{"id": "portsmouth-garage-renovation-overrun", "title": "Portsmouth Garage finished late and $4.5 million over its priority-work budget", "seconds": 56.2, "voice": "elevenlabs:iPYqcpY8j8Ap4jUf28I3", "narrator": "Michael", "tempo": 1.12, "made": "2026-11-25", "key": "587dfdfd29dd3489", "words": 150, "beats": [{"scene": "open", "kind": "hook", "ref": ["suspicious[0]", "established[0]"], "text": "The Controller compared the renovation’s cost with the budget for priority work.", "t0": 0.2, "t1": 4.2, "shot": "r0", "visual": {"type": "hook", "words": ["How", "much", "did", "the", "renovation", "cost?"], "sub": "Portsmouth garage"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.12, 0.56, 0.99, 1.09, 1.7, 2.37, 2.56, 2.67, 3.02, 3.18, 3.65]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "record", "ref": ["suspicious[0]", "established[0]"], "text": "About 13.2 million dollars was spent against an 8.7 million dollar priority-work budget.", "t0": 4.32, "t1": 10.71, "shot": "r1", "visual": {"type": "record", "layout": "amounts", "context": "April 2017 benchmark", "heading": "Priority work and actual spending", "source": "audit", "rows": [{"icon": "file", "label": "Priority-work budget", "value": "$8.7 million"}, {"icon": "transfer", "label": "Project expenses", "value": "$13.2 million"}]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.26, 0.73, 1.01, 1.33, 1.69, 2.45, 2.62, 2.87, 3.14, 3.32, 3.61, 3.94, 4.25, 4.55, 5.22, 5.98]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["suspicious[0]", "established[0]"], "text": "That was a 4.5 million dollar overrun against that benchmark.", "t0": 10.83, "t1": 14.69, "shot": "r2", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$4.5 million", "label": "Overrun against the priority-work budget"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.15, 0.28, 0.38, 0.62, 0.88, 1.26, 1.67, 1.99, 2.82, 3.14, 3.32]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["suspicious[0]", "established[0]"], "text": "The total budget also included money for contingencies and future work.", "t0": 14.81, "t1": 18.58, "shot": "r3", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "Contingencies and future work"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.15, 0.49, 0.87, 1.23, 1.64, 1.88, 2.02, 2.84, 3.11, 3.45]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "doc", "ref": ["established[1]"], "text": "The project schedule called for February 2019 completion. Occupancy was certified in April 2020.", "t0": 18.7, "t1": 25.65, "shot": "r4", "visual": {"type": "doc", "source": "audit", "kicker": "San Francisco Controller, City Services Auditor", "text": "Certificate of occupancy", "mark": "Certificate of occupancy"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.14, 0.51, 0.94, 1.32, 1.48, 2.05, 2.41, 2.92, 4.22, 4.91, 5.08, 5.63, 5.79, 6.24, 6.55]}, {"scene": "review", "kind": "doc", "ref": ["suspicious[1]", "established[2]"], "text": "Two firms answered the 2013 request. The board president overrode the selection panel.", "t0": 25.87, "t1": 31.2, "shot": "r5", "visual": {"type": "doc", "source": "audit", "kicker": "San Francisco Controller, City Services Auditor", "text": "First management award", "mark": "First management award"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.31, 0.8, 1.11, 1.21, 1.5, 1.96, 3.02, 3.16, 3.42, 3.87, 4.45, 4.56, 5.0]}, {"scene": "review", "kind": "doc", "ref": ["suspicious[2]", "established[3]"], "text": "The project architect reviewed five payment applications from the second contractor.", "t0": 31.32, "t1": 35.31, "shot": "r6", "visual": {"type": "doc", "source": "audit", "kicker": "San Francisco Controller, City Services Auditor", "text": "Five payment applications", "mark": "Five payment applications"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.12, 0.53, 1.02, 1.42, 1.8, 2.11, 2.78, 2.93, 3.03, 3.37]}, {"scene": "review", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["suspicious[2]", "established[3]"], "text": "The architect identified about 586,800 dollars in potential overbilling.", "t0": 35.43, "t1": 41.81, "shot": "r7", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$586,800", "label": "Architect’s estimate of potential overbillings"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.13, 0.66, 1.25, 1.59, 2.0, 2.33, 2.99, 3.79, 4.04, 4.33, 5.16, 5.36, 5.81]}, {"scene": "review", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["suspicious[2]", "established[3]"], "text": "The audit could not establish what action the corporation took on that review.", "t0": 41.93, "t1": 45.59, "shot": "r8", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "Payment applications"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.16, 0.45, 0.65, 0.88, 1.45, 1.65, 2.03, 2.13, 2.7, 2.92, 3.01, 3.2]}, {"scene": "review", "kind": "doc", "ref": ["established[4]"], "text": "The Controller later listed the report as closed in 2023.", "t0": 45.71, "t1": 49.58, "shot": "r9", "visual": {"type": "doc", "source": "closure", "kicker": "San Francisco Controller, City Services Auditor", "text": "July–December 2023", "mark": "July–December 2023"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.13, 0.66, 0.98, 1.31, 1.42, 1.91, 2.1, 2.63, 2.78, 3.1]}, {"scene": "review", "kind": "unknowns", "ref": ["notEstablished[0]"], "text": "The architect’s estimate does not establish a final amount due.", "t0": 49.7, "t1": 52.82, "shot": "r10", "visual": {"type": "unknowns", "cards": ["Payment reconciliation", "Recovery"]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.15, 0.64, 1.06, 1.3, 1.57, 2.07, 2.15, 2.43, 2.74]}, {"scene": "review", "kind": "end", "ref": ["status"], "text": "Every source is linked in the case file below.", "t0": 52.94, "t1": 55.3, "shot": "r11", "visual": {"type": "end"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.41, 0.82, 0.99, 1.26, 1.33, 1.43, 1.66, 1.93]}], "format": 6, "chapters": {"open": "The priority-work budget", "review": "The management and payment review"}, "look": "newsroom", "hook": "number"}